# Line endings.
#
# Text is stored as LF and checked out as LF. This belongs in the repository
# rather than in anyone's git config: this machine's *system* gitconfig sets
# core.autocrlf=true (the repo-local override says false), so a checkout made
# under that setting wrote ~1.8k files into the working tree as CRLF. Git hides
# those while their cached stat matches the index — and the moment any tool
# touches one, the entire file reappears as a few hundred lines of pure
# line-ending diff. Pinning the conversion here makes the index, the working
# tree and a fresh clone agree no matter what a local git config says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Deliberate CRLF: Windows batch files. cmd.exe seeks inside a batch file by
# byte offset, so `goto :label` — which the bin/*.cmd CLI wrappers use — is only
# reliable with CRLF. Only the checkout is affected; `text` still normalises the
# blob to LF, so the index does not change.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Committed binaries: never converted, never diffed as text. Every extension
# below exists in this tree; the artwork is the app's icons and the installer's
# branded bitmaps, which a text conversion would silently corrupt.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.bmp   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
# Assets.car is the macOS asset catalog.
*.car   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.node  binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.asar  binary
*.wasm  binary
